{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:45cf10d3c3b588ced46031be5bc5aa34ad34849d928b66eb831fd6482a0fbdf8","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026#thm:occupied","title":"Overlap on an arbitrary occupied board"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/9b43ba8f26252ced431a12f4.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:eb85d3603ec7254e8723f8292d2014fbb295087c537d4a9a7c22689061a82822","id":"r:Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026:thm:occupied","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026","name":"Overlap on an arbitrary occupied board","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"5.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/weighted.tex","label":"thm:occupied","line":96,"manuscript":"Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026","statement_sha256":"f74ca2512a59a581bc002bfad2d5e761efb9eb561f9e5e4ac19204f85c8550ed"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026.html#thm:occupied","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":5,"section_title":"Signed representations on occupied cells","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:83664e2bd83324559fc5bbfa62e7ec327bc13ab3afea17a8ae2953a5077d85e4","file":"preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/weighted.tex","line":96,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f74ca2512a59a581bc002bfad2d5e761efb9eb561f9e5e4ac19204f85c8550ed","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/weighted.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:83664e2bd83324559fc5bbfa62e7ec327bc13ab3afea17a8ae2953a5077d85e4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/weighted.tex#L96"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:occupied}\nTake a grid with \\(m\\) rows and \\(n\\) columns, \\(mn=N\\), and consider any subset of \\(s=N-t\\) cells, with the group \\(G_s\\) on those cells. Let \\(a\\vdash s\\) lie in the \\(h,h\\)-hook, \\(1\\le h\\le N\\). Decompose \\(V_a\\) under the within-row permutation subgroup of \\(G_s\\), and also (separately) the within-column subgroup. For types \\(\\sigma,\\theta\\) of these two groups, let \\(I_{\\sigma,u}: V_\\sigma\\to V_a\\), \\(I_{\\theta,v}: V_\\theta\\to V_a\\) be isometric embeddings giving orthogonal copies and spanning the respective isotypic spaces. Then\n\\begin{equation}\n \\sum_{u,v}\\|I_{\\sigma,u}^* I_{\\theta,v}\\|_\\infty^2\n \\ \\le\\\n \\exp\\{C[(m+n+1)h^2\\log(N+2)+t]\\}\\ \\min\\left\\{1,\\frac{D_\\sigma D_\\theta}{D_a}\\right\\}.       \\label{ten:weighted:eq:7}\n\\end{equation}\nHere \\(\\sigma\\) and \\(\\theta\\) can each consist of a tuple of partitions, and the infinity norm is the operator norm. For \\(s=0\\) the empty representation has dimension one."}
